.TH KVERIFY 1 "2026-06-27" "K-Verify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kverify \- Purple Team adversarial validation suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kverify
[\fI--scenario\fR \fIn\fR]
[\fI--list\fR]
[\fI--help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
K-Verify simulates 8 adversarial scenarios mapped to MITRE
ATT\&CK techniques and cross-validates detection by K-Scanner
and LinSpec. It performs synthetic RWX allocations, process
hiding, W^X bypass, ASLR checks, BPF validation, and YARA scans
to verify that the forensic ecosystem detects each technique.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--scenario \fIn\fR
Execute a single scenario (1-8).
.IP
1: RWX memory allocation (T1055)
.IP
2: Process masquerading (T1055.001)
.IP
3: W^X bypass via mprotect (T1055.001)
.IP
4: ASLR strength check
.IP
5: BPF filter presence check
.IP
6: YARA scan validation
.IP
7: K-Scanner cross-check
.IP
8: LinSpec cross-check
.TP
.B \--list
List all available scenarios with descriptions.
.TP
.B \--help
Display this help message and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, 1 on error or detection failure.
.SH BUGS
Some scenarios execute privileged operations (ptrace, prctl)
and must be run as root.
.SH AUTHOR
Jefferson Cesar Antunes
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kscanner (1),
.BR linspec (1),
.BR syscage (1)
